ing global signals from elementary events</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>91</volume><year>1997</year><fpage>367</fpage><lpage>373</lpage>a<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9363945</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Bootmanetal1997b"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bootman</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Niggli</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Berridge</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lipp</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Imaging the hierarchical Ca<sup>2+</sup> signaling system in HeLa cells</article-title><source>J. Physiol.</source><volume>499</volume><year>1997</year><fpage>307</fpage><lpage>314</lpage>b<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9080361</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CannellandSoeller1999"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cannell</surname><given-names>M.B.</given-names></name><name><surname>Soeller</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mechanisms underlying calcium sparks in cardiac muscle</article-title><source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source><volume>113</volume><year>1999</year><fpage>373</fpage><lpage>376</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10051513</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Chengetal1993"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cheng</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lederer</surname><given-names>W.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Cannell</surname><given-names>M.B.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Calcium sparkselementary events underlying excitation&#x02013;contraction coupling in heart muscle</article-title><source>Science.</source><volume>262</volume><year>1993</year><fpage>740</fpage><lpage>744</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8235594</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Chengetal19